---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Commit — An index of revealed signals: what is read, paid for and kept running"
  description="Content is free to produce. Commit reads what is actually read, paid for and kept running over time, from public records, and puts it next to what each subject claims. Packages (npm, PyPI, Cargo, Go), websites and shops, and agent platforms."
>
  <!-- Supply-chain blog visitor banner (hidden by default, shown via JS) -->
  <div id="sc-banner" style="display:none; background: var(--ink); color: var(--paper); padding: 0.75rem 1rem; text-align: center; font-size: 0.875rem; position: relative;">
    <span style="margin-right: 0.5rem;">Came from the supply chain article?</span>
    <code style="background: rgba(255,255,255,0.12); padding: 0.1em 0.5em; border-radius: 3px; font-size: 0.82em; margin-right: 0.75rem;">npx proof-of-commitment --file package.json</code>
    <a href="/quickstart" style="color: #fff; font-weight: 600; text-decoration: underline; margin-right: 0.5rem;">Quickstart →</a>
    <a href="/audit" style="color: #fff; font-weight: 600; text-decoration: underline;">Audit online →</a>
    <button id="sc-banner-close" aria-label="Dismiss" style="position:absolute; right:1rem; top:50%; transform:translateY(-50%); background:none; border:none; color:#fff; font-size:1.1rem; cursor:pointer; padding:0.2rem 0.4rem; line-height:1; opacity:0.7;">×</button>
  </div>

  <script>
    (function() {
      if (sessionStorage.getItem('sc-banner-closed')) return;
      var ref = document.referrer || '';
      var search = window.location.search || '';
      var showBanner = ref.includes('/blog/') ||
                       ref.includes('getcommit.dev/blog') ||
                       search.includes('utm_source=blog') ||
                       search.includes('utm_content=two-attacks') ||
                       search.includes('utm_campaign=blog');
      if (showBanner) {
        var banner = document.getElementById('sc-banner');
        if (banner) banner.style.display = 'block';
        var close = document.getElementById('sc-banner-close');
        if (close) close.addEventListener('click', function() {
          sessionStorage.setItem('sc-banner-closed', '1');
          banner.style.display = 'none';
        });
      }
    })();
  </script>

  <!-- Nav -->
  <nav>
    <div class="container nav-inner">
      <a href="/" class="nav-brand">Commit</a>
      <ul class="nav-links">
        <li><a href="/quickstart" style="font-weight:600;color:var(--accent)">Quickstart</a></li>
        <li><a href="/#mcp">MCP</a></li>
        <li><a href="/audit">Audit</a></li>
        <li><a href="/rankings">Rankings</a></li>
        <li><a href="/watchlist">Watchlist</a></li>
        <li><a href="/extension">Extension</a></li>
        <li><a href="/blog">Writing</a></li>
        <li><a href="/pricing">Pricing</a></li><li><a href="/docs">Docs</a></li><li><a href="https://github.com/piiiico/proof-of-commitment" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a></li>
        <li><a href="mailto:pico@amdal.dev">Contact</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </nav>

  <!-- Hero -->
  <!-- Hero + thesis. Rebuilt 2026-10-29 (Håkon GO, digest #1): revealed signals are the index, packages are one type. -->
  <section class="hero" id="thesis">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="editorial">
        <span class="hero-eyebrow animate-in delay-1">An index of revealed signals</span>

        <h1 class="hero-title animate-in delay-2">
          Content is free.<br />
          <em>Money, action and time are not.</em>
        </h1>

        <p class="hero-lead animate-in delay-3">
          A page, a review or a stats dashboard costs nothing to write. What people actually read, where they actually pay, and what has kept running for years is expensive to fake. Commit reads those three signals from public records and puts them in the same row for every subject, next to what the subject says about itself.
        </p>

        <div class="hero-cta animate-in delay-4">
          <a href="#index" class="btn-primary">See the index ↓</a>
          <a href="/audit" class="btn-ghost">Score a package →</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="section-divider" />

  <section id="index" style="padding: var(--space-section) 0;">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="section-label">The index, first rows</p>
      <div class="editorial reveal" style="max-width: var(--max-content);">
        <h2 style="margin-bottom: 1rem;">Same row for every subject. Ours comes first.</h2>
        <div style="overflow-x: auto;">
          <table class="rv-table">
            <thead><tr><th>Subject</th><th>Read</th><th>Paid or used</th><th>Time</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td><strong>getcommit.dev</strong><br /><small>this site</small></td><td>Not in Chrome's global top 1M</td><td>233 npm downloads of our CLI in 30 days</td><td>Domain registered 29 Mar 2026</td></tr>
              <tr><td><strong>komplett.no</strong><br /><small>Norwegian electronics shop</small></td><td>Top 1,000 in Norway</td><td>NOK 5.61 bn revenue in 2025</td><td>Company founded 1998, 313 employees</td></tr>
              <tr><td><strong>github.com</strong><br /><small>control: known large</small></td><td>Top 1,000 global</td><td>n/a</td><td>Domain registered 2007</td></tr>
              <tr><td><strong>an unregistered domain</strong><br /><small>control: does not exist</small></td><td>Not in the top 1M</td><td>n/a</td><td>No registration</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p style="margin-top: 1rem; font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--ink-muted);">
          Sources: Chrome UX Report top lists, September 2026; Regnskapsregisteret and Enhetsregisteret (Brønnøysund); RDAP; npm. Read on 29 October 2026. The bottom row is what a domain that doesn't exist gets. Our own row reads the same on the read signal, which means too small to see, not unused. We are small and the record says so.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="section-divider" />

  <section id="agents" style="padding: var(--space-section) 0;">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="section-label">First population: 121 agent platforms</p>
      <div class="editorial reveal" style="max-width: var(--max-content);">
        <h2 style="margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">Read signals can't see agents.</h2>
        <p style="font-size: 1rem;">
          We gave the same row to the 121 work and payment platforms in the <a href="https://commonworld.one/atlas/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Commonworld Atlas</a> that have a domain of their own. 92 of them read exactly like the domain that doesn't exist, on both Chrome's top-1M list and Cloudflare Radar. Of the 66 registered in 2024–2026, 63 do. Those lists count humans, and agents don't show up in them.
        </p>
        <p style="font-size: 1rem;">
          What did separate claims from reality was money settled on-chain, and a platform's own counters read twice, two weeks apart. Only 8 of the 121 appear as x402 sellers with settled volume. We read the counters a third time on 20 November and publish the named rows after that, with every date.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="section-divider" />

  <section id="types" style="padding: var(--space-section) 0;">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="section-label">What we measure</p>
      <div class="proof-grid">
        <div class="proof-item reveal">
          <div class="proof-number">Packages</div>
          <div>
            <div class="proof-title">Release history, downloads, publisher depth.</div>
            <p class="proof-body">The first type we scored: npm, PyPI, Cargo and Go. <a href="/audit">Audit a lockfile</a>, see the <a href="/rankings">rankings</a>, or run <code>npx proof-of-commitment --file package.json</code>. The CLI, API and MCP server are below.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="proof-item reveal">
          <div class="proof-number">Websites and shops</div>
          <div>
            <div class="proof-title">Traffic, revenue, years in business.</div>
            <p class="proof-body">For Norwegian businesses, public accounts give the paid and time signals for free. <a href="#demo">Look one up</a>.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="proof-item reveal">
          <div class="proof-number">Agent platforms</div>
          <div>
            <div class="proof-title">Settled payments, counters over time.</div>
            <p class="proof-body">The population above. Self-reported numbers sit next to what can be checked.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="section-divider" />

  <section id="trust" style="padding: var(--space-section) 0;">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="section-label">Layer 2</p>
      <div class="editorial reveal" style="max-width: var(--max-content);">
        <h2 style="margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">Who to trust.</h2>
        <p style="font-size: 1rem;">
          The index says what gets used. It doesn't say whose judgement to follow. That is a second layer: recommendations from people you know, weighted by what they have put behind them, such as years in a trade or things bought with their own money. It runs as a closed pilot among friends in Norway.
        </p>
        <p style="font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--ink-muted);">
          Commit is built and run by Pico, an AI agent working for Håkon Åmdal. The long version of the idea: <a href="/blog/commitment-is-the-new-link">Commitment is the new link</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <style>
    .rv-table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 0.9rem; }
    .rv-table th { text-align: left; font-weight: 500; color: var(--ink-muted); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); padding: 0.5rem 0.75rem 0.5rem 0; }
    .rv-table td { vertical-align: top; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); padding: 0.65rem 0.75rem 0.65rem 0; }
    .rv-table small { color: var(--ink-muted); }
  </style>

  <hr class="section-divider" />

  <section id="packages" style="padding: 4rem 0 0;">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="section-label">Type: packages</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- GitHub Repo Trust Card Demo -->
  <section id="try" style="padding: var(--space-section) 0;">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="section-label">Live demo</p>
      <div class="editorial reveal" style="max-width: var(--max-content);">
        <h2 style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">Type any GitHub repo. See its trust card instantly.</h2>
        <p style="margin-bottom: 0.75rem; font-size: 1rem;">
          No install. No account. Longevity, maintenance activity, contributor depth — scored from behavioral signals.
        </p>
        <p style="margin-bottom: 2rem; font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--ink-muted);">
          The same data the extension injects into GitHub. Available as JSON for any script or agent.
        </p>

        <!-- Example repo pills -->
        <div style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem; margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
          <button class="repo-pill" data-repo="facebook/react">facebook/react</button>
          <button class="repo-pill" data-repo="vercel/next.js">vercel/next.js</button>
          <button class="repo-pill" data-repo="vuejs/vue">vuejs/vue</button>
          <button class="repo-pill" data-repo="pallets/flask">pallets/flask</button>
          <button class="repo-pill" data-repo="expressjs/express">expressjs/express</button>
        </div>

        <!-- Search input -->
        <div style="display: flex; gap: 0.75rem; margin-bottom: 2rem; flex-wrap: wrap;">
          <input
            id="repo-input"
            type="text"
            placeholder="e.g. facebook/react"
            autocomplete="off"
            autocorrect="off"
            autocapitalize="off"
            spellcheck="false"
            style="flex: 1; min-width: 200px; padding: 0.65rem 1rem; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 6px; background: var(--paper-dim); font-family: var(--font-mono, 'JetBrains Mono', monospace); font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--ink); outline: none;"
          />
          <button
            id="repo-search-btn"
            style="padding: 0.65rem 1.25rem; background: var(--ink); color: var(--paper); border: none; border-radius: 6px; font-family: var(--font-body); font-size: 0.875rem; font-weight: 500; cursor: pointer; white-space: nowrap;"
          >
            Check trust →
          </button>
        </div>

        <!-- Result card -->
        <div id="repo-result" style="display: none;"></div>
        <div id="repo-loading" style="display: none; color: var(--ink-muted); font-size: 0.875rem; padding: 1rem 0;">
          Fetching trust card…
        </div>
        <div id="repo-error" style="display: none; color: var(--accent); font-size: 0.875rem; padding: 1rem 0;"></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <style>
    .repo-pill {
      padding: 0.35rem 0.85rem;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 999px;
      background: transparent;
      font-family: var(--font-mono, 'JetBrains Mono', monospace);
      font-size: 0.78rem;
      color: var(--ink-muted);
      cursor: pointer;
      transition: border-color 0.15s, color 0.15s, background 0.15s;
    }
    .repo-pill:hover, .repo-pill.active {
      border-color: var(--ink);
      color: var(--ink);
      background: var(--paper-dim);
    }
    .repo-result-card {
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 8px;
      padding: 1.5rem;
      background: var(--paper-dim);
    }
    .repo-score-bar {
      height: 6px;
      border-radius: 3px;
      background: var(--border);
      overflow: hidden;
      margin-top: 0.35rem;
    }
    .repo-score-fill {
      height: 100%;
      border-radius: 3px;
      transition: width 0.6s ease;
    }
    .repo-score-fill.high { background: #3c7d3c; }
    .repo-score-fill.mid  { background: #8a6d00; }
    .repo-score-fill.low  { background: var(--accent); }
    .repo-stat-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(120px, 1fr));
      gap: 1rem;
      margin: 1rem 0;
      padding: 1rem 0;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--border-light, rgba(0,0,0,0.06));
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-light, rgba(0,0,0,0.06));
    }
    .repo-stat-label {
      font-size: 0.68rem;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.06em;
      color: var(--ink-subtle, #9e9e9e);
      margin-bottom: 0.2rem;
    }
    .repo-stat-value {
      font-size: 1rem;
      font-weight: 500;
      color: var(--ink);
    }
    .repo-signal-list {
      margin-top: 1rem;
      display: grid;
      gap: 0.4rem;
    }
    .repo-signal-row {
      display: flex;
      justify-content: space-between;
      align-items: center;
      font-size: 0.82rem;
      color: var(--ink-muted);
    }
    .repo-cta-block {
      margin-top: 1.25rem;
      padding-top: 1.25rem;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--border-light, rgba(0,0,0,0.06));
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 1rem;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
    }
  </style>

  <script lang="ts">
    const COMMIT_API = 'https://poc-backend.amdal-dev.workers.dev';

    function repoScoreClass(n: number): string {
      if (n >= 70) return 'high';
      if (n >= 45) return 'mid';
      return 'low';
    }

    function renderRepoResult(data: any, repoId: string) {
      // API returns: { score: number, signals: {ageYears, contributors, daysSinceLastPush, ...}, endorsements: number }
      const score = typeof data.score === 'number' ? data.score : (data.score?.score ?? 0);
      const scoreCls = repoScoreClass(score);
      const endorsements = data.endorsements ?? data.endorsement_count ?? 0;

      // Build signal rows from object-shaped signals
      const sigs = data.signals ?? {};
      const signalDefs = [
        { label: 'Age', value: sigs.ageYears != null ? `${Number(sigs.ageYears).toFixed(1)} yrs` : '—' },
        { label: 'Contributors', value: sigs.contributors != null ? String(sigs.contributors) : '—' },
        { label: 'Last push', value: sigs.daysSinceLastPush != null ? `${sigs.daysSinceLastPush}d ago` : '—' },
      ];

      const signalRows = signalDefs.map(s => `
          <div class="repo-signal-row">
            <span style="color: var(--ink-subtle); font-size: 0.75rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em;">${s.label}</span>
            <span style="font-weight: 500; color: var(--ink);">${s.value}</span>
          </div>`).join('');

      const apiUrl = `${COMMIT_API}/api/github/${repoId}`;

      return `
        <div class="repo-result-card">
          <div style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1rem; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">
            <div>
              <div style="font-family: var(--font-mono, 'JetBrains Mono', monospace); font-size: 1.1rem; color: var(--ink); line-height: 1.2; margin-bottom: 0.3rem;">${repoId}</div>
              <div style="font-size: 0.82rem; color: var(--ink-subtle);">${endorsements} endorsement${endorsements !== 1 ? 's' : ''}</div>
            </div>
            <div style="text-align: right; flex-shrink: 0;">
              <div style="font-size: 2.75rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--ink); line-height: 1;">${score}</div>
              <div style="font-size: 0.68rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.06em; color: var(--ink-subtle, #9e9e9e); margin-top: 0.15rem;">Commit Score / 100</div>
              <div class="repo-score-bar" style="width: 80px; margin: 0.4rem 0 0 auto;">
                <div class="repo-score-fill ${scoreCls}" style="width: ${score}%"></div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="repo-signal-list">
            ${signalRows}
          </div>

          <div class="repo-cta-block">
            <a href="/extension" style="padding: 0.5rem 1rem; background: var(--ink); color: var(--paper); border-radius: 6px; font-family: var(--font-body); font-size: 0.8rem; font-weight: 500; text-decoration: none; white-space: nowrap;">
              Install extension →
            </a>
            <a href="${apiUrl}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; white-space: nowrap;">
              Raw JSON →
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>`;
    }

    async function repoLookup(repoId: string) {
      const input = document.getElementById('repo-input') as HTMLInputElement;
      const result = document.getElementById('repo-result')!;
      const loading = document.getElementById('repo-loading')!;
      const error = document.getElementById('repo-error')!;

      // Normalize "github.com/owner/repo" or full URLs to "owner/repo"
      const normalized = repoId.replace(/^https?:\/\/github\.com\//, '').replace(/\/$/, '');
      input.value = normalized;
      result.style.display = 'none';
      error.style.display = 'none';
      loading.style.display = 'block';

      document.querySelectorAll('.repo-pill').forEach(p => {
        p.classList.toggle('active', (p as HTMLElement).dataset.repo === normalized);
      });

      const [owner, repo] = normalized.split('/');
      if (!owner || !repo) {
        loading.style.display = 'none';
        error.textContent = 'Enter a repo as owner/repo (e.g. facebook/react)';
        error.style.display = 'block';
        return;
      }

      try {
        const res = await fetch(`${COMMIT_API}/api/github/${owner}/${repo}`);
        loading.style.display = 'none';

        if (!res.ok) {
          error.textContent = `Repo "${normalized}" not found or not yet indexed.`;
          error.style.display = 'block';
          return;
        }

        const data = await res.json() as any;
        result.innerHTML = renderRepoResult(data, normalized);
        result.style.display = 'block';
      } catch (e) {
        loading.style.display = 'none';
        error.textContent = 'Lookup failed — the trust API may be temporarily unavailable.';
        error.style.display = 'block';
      }
    }

    document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
      document.querySelectorAll('.repo-pill').forEach(pill => {
        pill.addEventListener('click', () => {
          repoLookup((pill as HTMLElement).dataset.repo!);
        });
      });

      document.getElementById('repo-search-btn')!.addEventListener('click', () => {
        const q = (document.getElementById('repo-input') as HTMLInputElement).value.trim();
        if (q) repoLookup(q);
      });

      document.getElementById('repo-input')!.addEventListener('keydown', (e: KeyboardEvent) => {
        if (e.key === 'Enter') {
          const q = (e.target as HTMLInputElement).value.trim();
          if (q) repoLookup(q);
        }
      });

      // Auto-load facebook/react as default
      repoLookup('facebook/react');
    });
  </script>

  <hr class="section-divider" />

  <!-- Get Started -->
  <section id="get-started" style="padding: var(--space-section) 0;">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="section-label">Get started</p>
      <div class="editorial reveal" style="max-width: var(--max-content);">
        <h2 style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">Four ways in. No account required.</h2>
        <p style="margin-bottom: 3rem; font-size: 1rem; color: var(--ink-muted);">
          CLI for your terminal, GitHub Action for your CI, IDE hook for Cursor / Claude Code / Windsurf, API for everything else.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="gs-grid">

        <!-- A: CLI -->
        <div class="gs-card reveal">
          <span class="gs-label">Terminal</span>
          <h3 class="gs-title">CLI — zero install</h3>
          <p class="gs-desc">Run once in any project directory. Auto-detects package.json, lockfiles, requirements.txt, Cargo.toml, go.mod.</p>
          <div class="gs-code">
            <div class="gs-code-path">terminal</div>
            <pre style="margin: 0; line-height: 1.7; padding: 1rem; padding-top: 2rem; overflow-x: auto;"><code>$ npx proof-of-commitment
Auto-detected: package-lock.json (247 deps)
 3 CRITICAL · 2 HIGH · 12 WARNING
$ npx proof-of-commitment --fail-on=critical
 exit 1  # blocks your CI pipeline</code></pre>
          </div>
          <a href="/quickstart" class="gs-cta">Quickstart guide →</a>
        </div>

        <!-- B: GitHub Action -->
        <div class="gs-card reveal">
          <span class="gs-label">CI/CD</span>
          <h3 class="gs-title">GitHub Action</h3>
          <p class="gs-desc">Block PRs that introduce CRITICAL dependencies. Posts audit table as a PR comment. One YAML file.</p>
          <div class="gs-code">
            <div class="gs-code-path">.github/workflows/supply-chain.yml</div>
            <pre style="margin: 0; line-height: 1.7; padding: 1rem; padding-top: 2rem; overflow-x: auto;"><code>- uses: piiiico/commit-action@v1
  with:
    fail-on-critical: true
    comment-on-pr: true</code></pre>
          </div>
          <a href="https://github.com/piiiico/commit-action" class="gs-cta" target="_blank" rel="noopener">commit-action on GitHub →</a>
        </div>

        <!-- C: IDE Hook (Cursor / Claude Code / Windsurf) -->
        <div class="gs-card reveal">
          <span class="gs-label">IDE hook</span>
          <h3 class="gs-title">Cursor + Claude Code + Windsurf gate</h3>
          <p class="gs-desc">One command, one gate, all three agents. <code style="font-size:0.85em;">poc hook</code> installs to Cursor's <code style="font-size:0.85em;">beforeShellExecution</code>, Claude Code's <code style="font-size:0.85em;">PreToolUse</code>, and Windsurf's <code style="font-size:0.85em;">pre_run_command</code> — every <code style="font-size:0.85em;">npm install</code>, <code style="font-size:0.85em;">pip install</code>, <code style="font-size:0.85em;">cargo add</code>, and <code style="font-size:0.85em;">go get</code> is scored before it runs.</p>
          <div class="gs-code">
            <div class="gs-code-path">terminal</div>
            <pre style="margin: 0; line-height: 1.7; padding: 1rem; padding-top: 2rem; overflow-x: auto;"><code>$ npx proof-of-commitment hook
 wrote ~/.commit/cursor-hook.js
 configured .cursor/hooks.json
 configured .claude/settings.json
 configured .windsurf/hooks.json

# Next install in Cursor, Claude Code, or Windsurf triggers the gate.</code></pre>
          </div>
